[{:seon.task/name "a-lazy-read-records-into-the-read-it-belongs-to"
  :seon.task/plan "Root, from the owner, 2026-11-14: a missed read is a correctness bug; the cost work waits (\"Don't worry about a few ms ... We can optimize it later. Right now we dedupe and upgrade everyone\"). deps, after the fork bound. What exists: datahike.reads/with-reads binds di/*reads* to an atom while f runs, and the persistent-set index records each range it scans (di/record-read!). A lazy value made inside f and realized after f returns (an entity's attributes, a lazy seq of datoms) reads the index with *reads* unbound, so the read it belongs to never records that range, and a later change to those datoms reaches no reader. Change: a lazy read made while *reads* is bound captures the atom at its creation and records into it when realized; nothing else moves. Proof, red first: a read that returns a lazy seq of an entity's datoms, realized after with-reads returns, still has that entity's range in its reads. Held, not now (root, same day): the planner's seeks (query/execute.cljc:89, :215), and ranges replayed on a result-cache or search-memo hit. Those would let with-reads leave the planner and caches on (q over 680 tasks 10 us cached vs 1,158 us recording, root's db [M])."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.db-test/a-lazy-read-records-into-the-read-it-belongs-to}
  :seon.task/needs #{}}]
